
  THE GEOMETRY OF 6174 = 2^1 * 3^2 * 7^3

======================================================================

  I. THE THREE TRIPLES
  --------------------------------------------------

  6174 = 2^1 * 3^2 * 7^3

  Three triples (base, exponent, value):
  Triple A: (2, 1, 2)   — the DOUBLER at power 1
  Triple B: (3, 2, 9)   — the CURVER at power 2
  Triple C: (7, 3, 343) — the FORBIDDEN at power 3

  Product: 2 * 9 * 343 = 6174

  The exponent IS the position:
  1st Hurwitz prime (2) raised to 1st power
  2nd Hurwitz prime (3) raised to 2nd power
  3rd Hurwitz prime (7) raised to 3rd power

  All 6 orderings of exponents (1,2,3) on bases (2,3,7):
  2^1 * 3^2 * 7^3 =   6174 <== KAPREKAR FIXED POINT!
  2^1 * 3^3 * 7^2 =   2646
  2^2 * 3^1 * 7^3 =   4116
  2^2 * 3^3 * 7^1 =    756
  2^3 * 3^1 * 7^2 =   1176
  2^3 * 3^2 * 7^1 =    504

  II. THE DIGIT STRUCTURE
  --------------------------------------------------

  6174 in digits: 6, 1, 7, 4
  Digit sum: 6+1+7+4 = 18 = 2*3^2 = 2*9
  Digit product: 6*1*7*4 = 168 = |PSL(2,7)| = 4*42!

  REMARKABLE: digit_product(6174) = 168 = |PSL(2,7)| = 84*(3-1)
  84 = 2*42 = Hurwitz bound coefficient
  168 = maximum automorphisms of a genus-3 curve (Klein quartic)

  Each digit as Hurwitz factorization:
  6 = 2*3     (the GEOMETRIC BASE)
  1 = 1       (the IDENTITY)
  7 = 7       (the FORBIDDEN PRIME)
  4 = 2^2     (the DOUBLED DOUBLER)

  7641 - 1467 = 6174 (Kaprekar fixed point)
  7641 = 3 * 2547 = 3 * 3 * 849 = 9 * 849 = 9 * 3 * 283
  1467 = 3 * 489 = 3 * 3 * 163
  Both divisible by 9 = 3^2 (the CURVER squared)

